# behavior 1
# name: comment_anchor_tracks_edits
# provenance: Comment.h carries Anchor range boundaries; the comment must keep
#   pointing at the same text while other producers edit around it. Anchors are
#   boundaries with affinity and context, and an unresolvable anchor must be an
#   explicit outcome (S04-S06 own the affinity fix).
# status: desired
# scope: comments
# expect converged yes
# expect comment_anchor 0 2 l 1
# note: the document is built one character at a time, so the comment's range
#   start can name an entry that exists before the later characters do. The 'b'
#   is the second item this replica inserted, and once the document is "abcd" an
#   anchor on it must resolve to offset 1. Fields: buffer replica, item ordinal
#   (1-based, counted over the items that replica inserted), bias, expected
#   offset. The ordinal replaced a raw Lamport pair when P06a adopted
#   run-interval allocation: the behaviour under test is unchanged and the
#   position is now named the way the fixture means it.
#collabtext-trace 1
#model buffer
#label comment-anchor
#seed 42
#replicas 1
#net 50 200 500 1
edit 0 0 0 61
deliver 0 0
edit 0 1 1 62
edit 0 2 2 63
edit 0 3 3 64
